WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.990
Autumn.

2
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.790
A shop puts up the price of
a jacket by twenty per cent.

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.960
Then winter comes, and the
jacket goes into the sale:

4
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.620
twenty per cent off.

5
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.000
Shoppers shrug.

6
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.170
Up twenty, down twenty.

7
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.750
Surely that's just the
original price again?

8
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.630
Is it?

9
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.680
Or has the jacket ended up somewhere else?

10
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.770
In this mission, you'll write a
percentage change as a multiplier.

11
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.550
Up twenty per cent means
multiply by one point two.

12
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.350
Down twenty per cent means
multiply by nought point eight.

13
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.120
And you'll work out a percentage
change, percentage profit and loss,

14
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.900
and simple interest.

15
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.090
Your mission: decide whether the
price ends up back where it started.
